/**
 * ISO/IEC 27017:2026 — information security controls based on ISO/IEC 27002 for cloud
 * services (second edition, published 2026-07-27). It replaces ISO/IEC 27017:2015, which ISO
 * lists as withdrawn; the first edition stays available in iso27017Controls.ts (registry key
 * 'ISO 27017') for organizations still assessed against it.
 *
 * Structure checked on 2026-09-27 against the publisher's table of contents (IEC webstore
 * publication 115400 and its official preview) and the ISO Open Data deliverables record:
 *   - The normative references are ISO/IEC 22123-1 and ISO/IEC 27002:2022, so this edition
 *     follows the 2022 control set and its four themes: 5 Organizational, 6 People,
 *     7 Physical, 8 Technological.
 *   - Each of the 93 ISO/IEC 27002:2022 controls has its own section (5.1-5.37, 6.1-6.8,
 *     7.1-7.14, 8.1-8.34), and four cloud-specific controls are added: 5.38, 5.39, 8.35
 *     and 8.36.
 *
 * Id mapping: ISO27017-2026-<n> is section <n> of the standard; for the 93 that is also the
 * ISO/IEC 27002:2022 control number, so ISO27017-2026-8.24 pairs with ISO 27001 A.8.24. Ids
 * never contain a colon, because stored control names are "<controlId>: <name>" and the id is
 * read back up to the first colon. The "2026" segment keeps these ids distinct from the 2015
 * ids (ISO27017-<2013 clause>), so both editions can exist in one organization without their
 * controls or crosswalk rows colliding.
 *
 * Names: the 93 reuse the ISO 27001:2022 Annex A titles from iso27001Controls.ts, written out
 * here so this module has no dependency on that one. The four cloud-specific controls use
 * short titles that follow the headings in the standard's table of contents, and their
 * descriptions begin "Cloud-specific control (ISO/IEC 27017:2026 addition)."
 *
 * What could NOT be verified: the body of the standard is not public, including Annex A
 * (correspondence with the 2015 edition), Annex B (monitoring of cloud services) and which of
 * the 93 sections carry cloud-specific guidance. Every description, guidance, evidence and
 * test line below is this product's own cloud-security guidance, split into what the cloud
 * service customer and the cloud service provider each do. It is not the text of the
 * standard; verify it against the licensed standard before certification use.
 *
 * Subjects of the 2015 cloud-only controls: CLD.6.3.1 and CLD.9.5.1 have the same titles as
 * 5.38 and 8.35. The other five are covered here by subject rather than from Annex A: removal
 * of customer assets (CLD.8.1.5) under 5.11 and 8.10, virtual machine hardening (CLD.9.5.2)
 * under 8.9, administrator operational procedures (CLD.12.1.5) under 5.37, alignment of
 * virtual and physical network security (CLD.13.1.4) under 8.20, and monitoring of cloud
 * services (CLD.12.4.5, now an informative annex) under 8.16.
 */
